{
    "word": "ensouled",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                "word": "ensouled",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a14e354c-ea23-4824-8dbf-a2f3834dc157",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more ensouled"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "703677d7-418b-488a-ab40-b21176ab4c5f",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most ensouled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d39e0cc6-e832-307f-b87a-3ba40b40525c",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a soul or spirit; Having sentience, consciousness and will."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4411be9-aec3-4911-9a10-b69de6bedc4d",
                                "sense_id": "d39e0cc6-e832-307f-b87a-3ba40b40525c",
                                "text": "In any case, whether the mother gives birth to a single child or to \"identical twins.\" the result is the birth of one or more \"ensouled\" persons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5681dfa9-94ea-4508-ba19-c2e159b543a4",
                                "sense_id": "d39e0cc6-e832-307f-b87a-3ba40b40525c",
                                "text": "As with Plato, the beings inhabiting our world are not ensouled in the same degree: animals are not ensouled in the same manner as human beings; plants are even worse off because, unlike animals, they have no capacity for feeling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed10eb91-b9c0-44c6-ae7d-74a591da9a01",
                                "sense_id": "d39e0cc6-e832-307f-b87a-3ba40b40525c",
                                "text": "The universe if full of motion and full of souls, but some things are much more ensouled and causative of motion (more active) than other things."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd7ed3b3-e619-49dc-801d-72c28b9cd889",
                                "sense_id": "d39e0cc6-e832-307f-b87a-3ba40b40525c",
                                "text": "Of course, a maggot is no more ensouled than a tree; put it on a piece of rotting flesh, and it will eat."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3025f733-4f7f-399a-be5d-200d11f40dc7",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a spiritual aspect;"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eb0361e-6ffd-4f29-8a44-8788cc95033e",
                                "sense_id": "3025f733-4f7f-399a-be5d-200d11f40dc7",
                                "text": "More generally, one could say that through revealing a profound paralleling between the psychic and physical events, synchronicity as it were adds a missing half to each, making the psychic events more embodied and the physical events more ensouled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ad7b82f-78ff-4c5d-b664-d23b90e17149",
                                "sense_id": "3025f733-4f7f-399a-be5d-200d11f40dc7",
                                "text": "Influenced by both Plato and Aristotle, Plotinus' project involved bringing together the Phaedo's portrait of the soul as otherworldly with the Timaeus' more ensouled account of the material world. (Rist 1967, p. 112)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5a80bc-3969-4334-99e3-6c1cb960dabf",
                                "sense_id": "3025f733-4f7f-399a-be5d-200d11f40dc7",
                                "text": "La Brosse's notion of the soul is both specific to any given being—\"all subjects of nature have individual souls\"—and common to all beings without hierarchical distinction:\"[O]f all the souls that inhabit the universe, as forms that give being to things, some are not more ensouled than others, just as the life that results is not more lively in one subject than in another.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Full of soul; soulful; spiritually profound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "559959eb-4f65-412f-b3e9-d97225fa4136",
                                "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                                "text": "For a. more ensouled world, therefore, we need to embrace the qualities of old age, too, no matter how old we ourselves are; its ability to act from truth rather than expectation and its awareness of the frailty and fragility of life will assist us in understanding what really matters and the importance of love in our lives: the only truth that really matters."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15d210d2-b1c2-4f67-8b71-362c9bd61ab5",
                                "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                                "text": "A fundamental yet virtually unexamined issue . . . today is the question of whether all beauty. . . is merely a random product of blind evolution and subjective circumstance or whether that beauty is in some sense significant and intentional, and expression of something more ensouled, more profound, intelligently relational, mysterious."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e3383f8-10ef-496b-bc5f-a98ec1aa4888",
                                "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                                "text": "Something similar occurs with the life-processes, which are more ensouled in the enjoyment of art than they are in normal life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20b064b6-6bc6-46ad-935d-8d8746b885b2",
                                "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                                "text": "We simply feel, as some describe it, more whole, more complete, more ensouled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37ff77d1-0d63-41f8-870b-2a0329337928",
                                "sense_id": "21a5483b-946d-3834-bfab-5a5bde4e0ce4",
                                "text": "Or perhaps she was looking at personified figures who were dreaming her life toward—or into—death for the purpose of initiating the rebirth of life on a more conscious, and more ensouled, plane ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "884a73de-01f2-3797-a3cd-2990706c119d",
                        "entry_id": "c195cf1b-db2f-308f-8ed6-4cf8ecfb60b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Instilled into the soul; deep and inward."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "796e81f1-b0cf-45b9-8b9b-e6cb2ed9b349",
                                "sense_id": "884a73de-01f2-3797-a3cd-2990706c119d",
                                "text": "In this way, we can see how the son carries the mother's characteristics a step deeper so that they become a part of his consitution, whereas the daughter raises the father's characteristics a step so that they are more inward, more ensouled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2917162-ef64-4d79-b1aa-4f551c39f000",
                                "sense_id": "884a73de-01f2-3797-a3cd-2990706c119d",
                                "text": "We gain nothing by prescribing a fixed treatment regimen instead of an ensouled connection with each other, and we lose considerable insight into soul and psyche."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbb5b543-7f76-41f1-975e-ff89070b3054",
                                "sense_id": "884a73de-01f2-3797-a3cd-2990706c119d",
                                "text": "The history of the shaman gives us an image of the first historical human figure that we know of who was initially pat of a tribal culture, then alienated trough a destabilizing eruption of visionary material ('broken'), and finally reassembled through what appears to be a unique process of evolving ego capacity and a growing possibility of witnessing consciousness that made them whole again; not 'whole' as the shaman was before, but whole in a way that includes the molten gold of conscious suffering and the ensouled wisdom that suffering can bring."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
